EXTENSION "ArM5_Through_the_Aegis_NorthernSeas_VisSources" {
    NAME "Ars Magica Fifth Edition, Through the Aegis - Chapter Two: The Northern Seas vis sources"
    VERSION "0.5.1"
    SPEC_VERSION "0.5"
    RELEASE_DATE "2026-10-06"
    DEPENDS_ON "ArM5_Through_the_Aegis_Core_Ext"

    # The chapter's vis sources, structured; each DESCRIPTION the source's text, verbatim.

    #t67fcfc5b566276e5c7b905 ^"Fire From the Sky" DEF {
        EXTENDS #tOyKnFGWkxgPeCHccUaG06R3 ^"Vis Source"
        PROPERTIES {
            ^"Art" STRING "Terram"
            ^"Build Points" INTEGER 50
            ^"Source" STRING "Through the Aegis"
            ^"Page" INTEGER 31
        }
        DESCRIPTION "*10 Pawns of Terram per Year* Once a year, the freezing winds sweep down from the north and build over several days, culminating in a thunderous hail storm over the northern seas. In among the stinging hailstones are, on average, ten fist-sized spheres of burning granite that arrive out of the sky like thunderbolts.\n\nThe magi sail into the storm so that they can quickly locate the burning stones as they fall, using magic to capture them in the air, or to send divers down to the seabed to collect them.\n\nThe stones can damage any ships they strike, but the magi must sail close and act quick if they are to profit from the venture as the stones lose their vis if not collected within the night.\n\nThe storm always happens in winter, but it takes an Intelligence + Artes Liberales (Astrology) roll to determine where and how long the magi have to reach it. A low roll leaves the covenant little time to reach the site of the storm and the magi may need to find other ways to get there in time.\n\nThis source costs 50 Build Points."
    }

    #t52f2897e72b1aef4a5e2f1 ^"The Kraken’s Egg" DEF {
        EXTENDS #tOyKnFGWkxgPeCHccUaG06R3 ^"Vis Source"
        PROPERTIES {
            ^"Art" STRING "Animal"
            ^"Build Points" INTEGER 25
            ^"Source" STRING "Through the Aegis"
            ^"Page" INTEGER 31
        }
        DESCRIPTION "*5 Pawns of Animal each Year* A giant kraken rises from the deep every spring to feed and to lay a single egg. It arrives predictably enough two hundred miles southwest of La Rochelle, but it isn’t always clear where she’ll go.\n\nMagi may witness the kraken hunting whales or even ships, both of which form a season of useful insight for those studying Animal. This propensity to attack ships is a danger to the covenant, so magi would be advised not to sail too close and to consider strongly whether to intervene when another ship is attacked.\n\nEventually, at some point toward the end of the season, she dives again and leaves behind a single egg that floats on the tide. This\n\nsmooth translucent leathery pouch the size of a grain sack contains five pawns of Animal vis. If left in the sea, the egg develops into a new kraken that hatches the following year, losing the vis. If taken from the sea, the egg does not develop and the vis is preserved.\n\nThis source costs 25 Build Points."
    }

    #t9e5340bdc0899e78575bdf ^"The Summer Fog" DEF {
        EXTENDS #tOyKnFGWkxgPeCHccUaG06R3 ^"Vis Source"
        PROPERTIES {
            ^"Art" STRING "Rego, Auram, Mentem"
            ^"Build Points" INTEGER 25
            ^"Source" STRING "Through the Aegis"
            ^"Page" INTEGER 32
        }
        DESCRIPTION "*5 Pawns of Mentem vis each Year* On the last day of July, the inhabitants of the troubled village of Sønder Vorupør shut up their doors and windows against the horrors of the night, for a fog rolls in from the North Sea bringing nightmares with it.\n\nThose caught in the fog suffer the effect described below. Magi, however, may collect the fog, gaining on average five pawns of Mentem vis each year. Curiously, the vis itself does not appear to carry the effect, though taking the vis does dissipate it and save the villagers from their nightmares. The fog may be manipulated through Rego Auram effects and the vis is collected in large leather bags.\n\n**The Unbidden Horrors**\n\nCrMe 20 Pen +10, 1/day\n\nR: Touch, D: Sun, T: Individual Individuals touched by the fog feel unease, rising to dread, through suspicion and fear, and into the horror of their deepest nightmares. The effect lasts through the night, and the screams of those unlucky cursed few can be heard throughout the village of Sønder Vorupør.\n\nThe memories of the experience live longer than the effects of the magic itself.\n\n(Effect: Base 4, +1 Touch, +2 Sun; Modifications: +5 for +10 Penetration)\n\nThis source costs 25 Build Points."
    }

    #t8453864207fcd51c79130f ^"The Black Horse of Boulogne" DEF {
        EXTENDS #tOyKnFGWkxgPeCHccUaG06R3 ^"Vis Source"
        PROPERTIES {
            ^"Art" STRING "Rego"
            ^"Build Points" INTEGER 20
            ^"Source" STRING "Through the Aegis"
            ^"Page" INTEGER 32
        }
        DESCRIPTION "*Four pawns of Rego vis each year.* Otto-Pauels knows of a secret pool where a black stallion of enormous size comes every autumn. The horse is of such an unnatural blackness that it can scarcely been seen in the night when it comes. But the horse must once have been tamed for it wears shoes of iron.\n\nEach year, the stallion comes to the pool in the clearing and, invisible against the night, it drinks from the pool. If, during its visit, it spies a set of new iron shoes upon the ground, it throws off its old ones and stands upon the new. When the horse goes, it takes the new shoes with it and leaves a pawn of Rego vis in each of the discarded shoes.\n\nThe vis is tainted with the realm of faerie and Otto suspects that the horse is associated with a craftsman’s endeavors and gains something from the gift of finely-crafted new shoes.\n\nThis source is considered a *seisin* of The Northern Seas and is protected by Tribunal law.\n\nThis source costs 20 Build Points."
    }

}
